# REQUIRES: cuda
# The stop of the covering reach against the cell (D[md-alg-segments-build],
# as #795's): the 403 waters of Inputs/triclinic, whose least face width
# c_z = 1.8385 nm leaves half of it, 0.919 nm, below the largest covering
# reach of the list, 0.9 + 2 (0.09582) nm. The first build stops the run
# with both lengths.
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/segments_coverage.py system dodecahedron %S/../Driver/Inputs %t 10 --cell
# RUN: cd %t && mdir run control.toml > run.log
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/segments_coverage.py emit dodecahedron %S/../Driver/Inputs %t
# RUN: mdir-opt %t/harness.mlir --convert-md-exec-to-gpu --convert-md-alg-to-gpu \
# RUN: | mlir-opt %lower_gpu_to_llvm \
# RUN: | not mlir-runner -e main --entry-point-result=void --shared-libs=%mlir_c_runner_utils,%mdrt,%mdrt_cuda 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: the covering reach of the list of units, 10.92 Ang (the pair list distance plus twice 0.9582 Ang, the largest covering radius of its units), exceeds half the least face width of the cell, 9.192 Ang; the run has failed (use a larger cell)
